# Netlify redirects for appcoaching.io
#
# How routing works now:
# - Every real page is a static file generated at build time by
#   scripts/generate-static-shells.js (index.html, services.html, about.html, blog.html,
#   blog/<slug>.html, contact.html, privacy.html). Netlify serves "/services" straight from
#   "services.html", so no rewrite rule is needed for them.
# - Any URL that doesn't match a file gets build/404.html with a real HTTP 404 status
#   (Netlify does this automatically when a 404.html exists). That 404 page still loads
#   the React app, which shows a "page not found" view with links back into the site.
#
# The old catch-all rule ("/*  /index.html  200") was removed on purpose: it returned the
# homepage with a 200 status for every made-up URL (a "soft 404"), which wastes crawl budget
# and lets junk URLs get indexed. Do not re-add it. Do not add a "/blog/*" rule either.

# Trailing-slash variants → the canonical no-slash URL (one URL per page everywhere)
/services/      /services      301
/about/         /about         301
/blog/          /blog          301
/contact/       /contact       301
/privacy/       /privacy       301
/blog/:slug/    /blog/:slug    301
